 "result_text": "`to_dict()` no longer sends `null` for the structured metadata fields, so Studio's \"must pass a list of values\" check shouldn't reject topic nodes any more. I only confirmed that the module imports. I didn't run the test suite or try an upload.\n\nThe change is in `ricecooker/classes/nodes.py`:\n- **Topic nodes:** `TreeNode.to_dict()` now leaves out `grade_levels`, `resource_types`, `learning_activities`, `accessibility_categories`, `subjects` and `needs` entirely.\n- **Content nodes:** `ContentNode.to_dict()` drops any of those six keys whose value is `None`. A video with no `grade_levels` set would have hit the same Studio error, so I fixed it there too. Fields that are set still go out as lists.\n\nI added a module-level `_METADATA_KEYS` tuple listing the six fields, which the content-node filter uses.",
